      "message": "fix(motion): the plan's crossing check excuses only a chord end at the other chord's END point\n\nReview of #1134 (head d1dc959b): reading a chord end within TOUCH of the\nother chord's LINE as a touch hid a walk passing through a chord at a\nvertex a picometre off its interior (both of the walk's chords there\nread as touching). The guard now uses the verifier's end-point-only\nrule (#1129, CROSSING_TOUCH / proper_cross_touch): an end within 1 pm\nof one of the other chord's end points reads as on its line; away from\nend points the exact sign stays the law.\n\nPinned by a_walk_through_a_chord_at_a_vertex_a_picometre_off_its_line_still_crosses\n(+-0.5 pm, at 0 / 37 / 1000 mm origins); a_contact_is_no_crossing_and_a_micron_past_is\nnow pins that a vertex a rounding past a chord's interior crosses.\n\nRefs #1048\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
